# Line endings.
#
# Windows CI checks out with CRLF unless told otherwise, and `cargo fmt --check`
# then fails every Rust file with "Incorrect newline style". That is not a
# formatting problem in the source, it is a checkout artefact, and it turned the
# Windows leg of CI permanently red for a reason that has nothing to do with the
# code. Normalise text to LF in the working tree on every platform.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Binary, never normalised. Rewriting a byte inside any of these corrupts it.
*.png    binary
*.jpg    binary
*.jpeg   binary
*.webp   binary
*.icns   binary
*.woff2  binary
*.ttf    binary
*.raf    binary
*.arw    binary
*.cr2    binary
*.cr3    binary
*.nef    binary
*.orf    binary
*.dng    binary
*.pef    binary
*.rw2    binary
*.tiff   binary
*.dcp    binary
*.lblook binary
*.bundle binary
